Sure! Those coordinates point to the Googleplex in Mountain View, California.  
Below is a quick example of how you’d hit the Google Geocoding API to reverse‑geocode that latitude/longitude pair, and what the response looks like.

---

## 1. Make the API call

```http
GET https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json
    ?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499
    &key=YOUR_API_KEY
```

> **Tip:** Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with a valid Google Maps Platform API key that has the Geocoding API enabled.

---

